  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "The horizontal range and maximum height attained by a projectile are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>H</mi></math> respectively. If a constant horizontal acceleration <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> is imparted to the projectile due to wind, then its horizontal range and maximum height will be&nbsp;",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "xxWbm",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "fgIZU",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "EjrML",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>H</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "y8CCN",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mi>g</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Here maximum height will be same as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>H</mi></math>&nbsp;because there is no acceleration change in vertical direction.</p><p>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>T</mi></math></p><p>When a horizontal acceleration is also given to the projectile <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>H</mi></math> will remain&nbsp;unchanged while range will become</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mo>&#8757;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Therefore horizontal range &amp; maximum height will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>H</mi></math>.</p>",
